Maintainer: Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 2:1.21)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/andy-d-70/dnshived
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/andy-d-70/dnshived.git

Package: dnshived
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, adduser, iproute2
Recommends: dnsmasq-base, keepalived, nftables
Description: Clustered DNS/DHCP reliability appliance
 dnshived is a lightweight, deterministic HA DNS/DHCP platform
 for VLAN-heavy networks, AV/IoT environments, and SMB datacenters.
 .
 Every core node is symmetric (core-1/core-2/core-3); ownership is
 gated by a five-part safety predicate (quorum, authoritative
 desired state, valid lease, unfenced token, arbiter-granted witness) so a
 scope is never served by two nodes at once. The same package installs on
 every node, including probe hosts — real role is set purely by which
 config file ends up written (/etc/dnshived/cluster.json for a core
 role, /etc/dnshived/probe.json for a probe), never by which binaries
 happen to be present. dnsmasq/keepalived/nftables are Recommends, not
 hard Depends, since a probe-only node never needs them.
 .
 Includes the privileged helper (dnshived-helper), the standalone operator
 web UI (dnshived-web), the interactive console (dnshived-top), a
 Nagios-compatible monitor (dnshived-status), the invariant validation
 framework (dnshived-validate), a DHCP dual-active detector
 (dnshived-dhcp-probe), a BOOTP/DHCP relay agent (dnshived-relay), a DNS
 relay (dnshived-dnsrelay), and the probe host itself (dnshived-probe +
 its privileged companion dnshived-probe-helper) — none of the
 non-always-on units start by default, all are opt-in/config-driven.
 .
 Every bootstrap-capable daemon (dnshived, dnshived-helper, dnshived-probe,
 dnshived-probe-helper) is enabled and started on a fresh install,
 sitting in its own independent, unauthenticated bootstrap mode until
 something configures it. Configuring one role (writing cluster.json OR
 probe.json) stops and disables whichever OTHER role's daemon pair is
 now irrelevant on this same host — a node can never simultaneously
 believe it's both a core role and a probe.
